{
  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "Completed runs show RNA-only multiprofile scvi_n200 with avgpool is the clear best unimodal setting, with 0.650 accuracy and 0.628 F1, while image-only ResNet50 is weak at 0.208 accuracy. This leaves important uncertainty about whether image features can add value when fused with the strongest RNA representation. config_030 keeps the best RNA settings fixed and adds only a ResNet50 image branch with simple concat fusion, so it directly tests the effect of adding image/fusion relative to the best unimodal baseline. This is the best next experiment because it exploits the strongest existing direction while minimally exploring the central multimodal/fusion question; if it improves, it identifies a promising multimodal path, and if it does not, it discourages more complex multimodal variants."
}

